<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lavrentiy Beria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lavrenti Beria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lavrentiy Beria was a Georgian Bolshevik and Soviet security chief. He led the Communist Party of the Transcaucasian SFSR and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from the early 1930s, carrying out the purges there, and in 1938 became head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> under Stalin, running the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulag">Gulag</a> and mass repressions. He also oversaw the Soviet atomic bomb project. After Stalin's death he was arrested and executed in 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lavrentiy-beria.jpg" alt="Lavrentiy Beria" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, presumed official · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lavrentiy_Beria_portrait_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
